      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "require 'prime'\n\ns, a, b = gets.split.map { |x| x.to_i }\n\nfac_a = Prime.prime_division(a).to_h\nfac_b = Prime.prime_division(b).to_h\n\nkeys = fac_a.keys | fac_b.keys\n\nGCD = {}\nLCD = {}\n\nkeys.each do |k|\n  av = fac_a.fetch(k, 0)\n  bv = fac_b.fetch(k, 0)\n  GCD[k] = [av, bv].min\n  LCD[k] = [av, bv].max\nend\n\ngcd = Prime.int_from_prime_division(GCD.to_a)\nlcd = Prime.int_from_prime_division(LCD.to_a)\n\nif s == 1 \n    puts lcd\nelse \n    puts gcd\nend\n",
      "statement": "For positive integers [[a]] and [[b]]:\nThe  <<Greatest Common Divisor>>,  gcd([[a]],[[b]]) is the largest integer [[c]], so that [[c]] divides both [[a]] and [[b]].\nThe <<Least Common Multiple>>, lcm([[a]],[[b]])  is the smallest integer [[c]], so that [[a]] and [[b]] both divide [[c]].",
